er-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2708eacc-b12f-5049-bb93-6886b57484fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-111185" :question/problem "The point $P$ with coordinates $(3,6)$ lies on the curve $y=f(x).$ Which of the following points must lie on $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "The function $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(x)$ represents a compression of the function $y=f(x)$ by a factor of $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis. This has the effect of dividing the $y$-coordinates of all points on $y=f(x)$ by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the point $(3,6)$ on $f(x)$ is mapped to the point $(3,\\frac{6}{3})=(3,2),$ and this point must lie on the graph of $y=\\frac{1}{3}f(x).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101246 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100985 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "0dd2eb6c-270f-5537-96f3-5c5438966eab" :knowledge-point/title "Plotting the Graph of a Vertically Stretched Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "da1ff81d-d04e-52ec-ab32-281987508598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9d365b79ff824808c9fd0f9177f234d4cad90eeeb1a5d0375e32331aa06226c6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098808} {:answer/id #uuid "006ea1df-160d-5e03-a362-bff668361f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/13/1309614901d95ce5ff95309d1614987e9f321749e2a64a4b77408101a4746a81.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098809} {:answer/id #uuid "2a493576-895f-56ef-b37c-f24370c67f4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/fd/fdc7faf421e1e594ab729eb741c8f5c68bcb61924e73f2252509d8074a03035c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186098810} {:answer/id #uuid "2b50950d-3c8b-5932-8bd9-48f72308